// The hand-scored plain-language sample (roadmap 1.5, the plain-language
// pass; design skill `copy/Vocabulary.prompt.md`). Every row is one card
// from the recorded sessions under `tests/fixtures/replay/` - the two real
// dogfood exports (`sep14-real`, `sep04-real`), the two reconstructions and
// the synthetic Claude-served recording (`sep26-claude`) - read by hand against the vocabulary's one rule: a card is plain when
// the sentence around every technical name would still be understood
// without it, and a never-say word stands only where the person chose the
// thing, where it is the thing itself in mono, or inside <details>. The
// pre-pass that listed candidate words was an aid; each label is a reading.
// `key` is sha256(title\nbody) truncated to 12, so a label can never drift
// onto another card, and a card with no row is unknown - out of the
// denominator, never a negative (`plain_language_share`,
// `scripts/interaction-metrics.ts`). The sample's number is the starting
// line: the recorded evenings predate the rule, and every real card leans
// on a word from the table. A new recording under contract 4.0 is labelled
// the same way, one row per card, and is where the number moves.
// A card the app authors that no recording holds yet is labelled from the
// end-to-end spec that shows it (git integration PR 1.3): its row names
// that spec in `from`, and the spec reads the card off the running app and
// fails when its words no longer match a row - so a copy change to the
// card is read again by hand before it ships. Only the app's own words are
// labelled this way; a card a spec scripts for its mock model measures
// nothing about the app.
// Each recorded card's row carries a second reading (contract 4.58,
// FI3-542): `clear` is true when the card's open prose - outside <details>,
// figures and code - follows the five sentence habits `CARD_AUTHORING`
// states, and false when one is broken; `clear_note` names what broke. A
// habit is broken by a sentence over 25 words (text in quotes or in
// parentheses, a number and an identifier each count as one word) or one
// holding three or more facts; by one thing under two names or one name for
// two things; by a passive that hides who did the work when the author or
// the reader's next step is the doer (a state such as "is merged" is not
// one); by a figure of speech; or by three or more actions chained in one
// sentence instead of a numbered list. The word count was an aid; each
// label is a reading. `clear_copy_share` scores it, and a row with no
// `clear` is out of its denominator.
// A recorded card whose body names a pull request carries a third reading
// (FI3-1307): `pr_links` is true when every pull request the body names -
// by its number or by its address - is a link that opens that pull
// request's page, and false when one is text or a link that opens nothing;
// `pr_links_note` names which. A card whose body names none carries no
// `pr_links`, and neither does one whose title alone names one: a title
// holds no link. An action id that spells a number (`merge-pr55`) names no
// pull request. `pr_link_share` scores it.
